---
import PublicLayout from "~/layouts/PublicLayout.astro";
---

<PublicLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What Aigenvora collects, why, and how long it's kept — in plain language."
>
  <article class="container legal">
    <p class="mono-label">Privacy · plain language</p>
    <h1>What we collect, and why.</h1>

    <h2>Browsing this site</h2>
    <p>
      This site sets no cookies, runs no third-party analytics and does no fingerprinting. Pages
      are served with standard web server logs (IP address, user agent, requested page) kept for
      operational security and rotated automatically. If we later add first-party visit counting,
      this page will describe exactly what it stores before it goes live.
    </p>

    <h2>The contact form</h2>
    <p>
      When you write to us we store what you submit — name, email, company, and your message —
      plus the page you sent it from and, when your browser passes them, campaign parameters. We
      use it to reply and to keep track of the conversation. We don't sell it, share it, or add
      you to a mailing list you didn't ask for.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>
      Lead records are kept while a conversation or engagement is live and deleted on request —
      write to <a href="mailto:hello@aigenvora.com">hello@aigenvora.com</a> and we'll confirm
      removal within a week.
    </p>

    <h2>Where data lives</h2>
    <p>
      Submissions are stored in Google Cloud Firestore under access controls limited to Aigenvora.
      Nothing you send through this site is used to train AI models.
    </p>

    <p class="mono-label updated">Last updated 2026-09-01</p>
  </article>
</PublicLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding-block: var(--space-stage) var(--space-5);
    max-width: 72ch;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-display);
    margin-block: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    margin-block: var(--space-3) var(--space-1);
  }
  p {
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  a {
    color: var(--accent-electric);
  }
  .updated {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }
</style>
